{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENUJwLanhTTSj36n9wU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are now wired into the registration and offers screens through `Analytics.capture`. `flutter analyze` reports no issues and the formatter needs no changes. I did not run the app or check events in PostHog. Nothing is committed.\n\n**What fires where**\n- `registration_email_started` and `registration_phone_started`: on the first edit of each field, per screen visit.\n- `loan_amount_changed` (`amount`): once per slider drag, when the user lets go.\n- `terms_accepted`: when the checkbox becomes ticked.\n- `registration_continue_tapped` (`amount`, `terms`): on Continue, before navigating.\n- `offers_scrolled` (`offset`): once per scroll gesture, using `ScrollEndNotification`.\n\nNo email or phone values are sent.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied three parts: once-per-visit flags for the text fields, `onChangeEnd` for the slider, and `ScrollEndNotification` for scrolls. The other parts did not apply, since no event needs a final value and the spec allows no per-change events. The dashboard checks were not done because I had no device or PostHog access. ANSWER.md lists this in full.\n\n**Decisions to review**\n- A tap on the slider with no movement still sends `loan_amount_changed`, because Flutter calls `onChangeEnd` on a tap. The spec says \"moved\", so a guard may be wanted.\n- `terms_accepted` fires on every tick, so untick and re-tick sends two events.\n- `offers_scrolled` reports the final pixel position, not the distance scrolled.\n\n`flutter pub get` altered `analysis_options.yaml` and created `pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool/`. I reverted and removed those, so the diff is only the two screen files plus `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2250,"cache_read